---
description: Airside shared working rules — read AGENTS.md and GAME.md first
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` and `GAME.md` at the repo root before making changes — they are
the shared contract for every contributor (Bailey, ChatGPT, Cursor, Codex, Claude)
and override anything else.

Key points:

- The Unity game lives in `game/Airside/` (Unity 6.3 LTS). Open that folder in Unity.
- The git repo is the single source of truth, hosted at `github.com/Bazlinka/Airside`
  (private, remote `origin`). `git pull --rebase origin main` before work; keep
  commits narrow; update `GAME.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` in the same commit; push to
  `origin` straight after.
- One change, one owner. Use a `feature/<name>` branch or worktree for parallel
  work with non-overlapping files.
- Domain/Simulation code stays independent of Unity scenes. Injected clock, seeded
  random, reserve runways/taxiways/stands before use, frame rate must not change
  simulation outcomes, preserve save compatibility.
- Run `scripts/test-unity.sh` and confirm the project compiles in Unity 6.3 LTS
  before committing behaviour changes. No merge rests on an unverified claim that
  a build passed.
